A||||2||BAM-BAM||Poly bushing replacement....to easy!||||12||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||07-17-2000||02:59 PM||||  Well I have done it, I have replace the old worn out rubber bushings with new Polyurethane bushings. I was kind of aprehensive at first because everyone made  it sound difficult to remove the old rubber bushings. Some said that they had to be burned out, others suggested using liquid nitrogen, and even some recomended hammering them out. Well, I did none of those, not because I thought they were wrong, merely because I had no torch, no access to liquid nitrogen or a big enough hammer. Insted I used a drill, a screwdriver and a pair of visegrip pliers. It all took me about an hour, and most of that was just the proccess of planning. It took less than five minutes per bushing. The upper bushings took under two minutes each. Oh, I also used a small hammer and a razor knife. It was almost to easy. <P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000001||mshill||07-18-2000||02:37 AM||||I have done the front bushings on two cars now and definitely prefer the drilling method to the burning method.  It is faster, cleaner and doesn't smell nearly as bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||07-18-2000||07:46 AM||||  Thank you, I couldn't believe how easy it was. I used a razor knife to peel off the flanged rubber edges, then I used a drill with a 3/16-1/4 bit and drilled several holes around the center pin hole, being careful to stay as close to the center pin as possible. Then, aggressively hammered on the center pin untill I had enough pushed out to grab onto with the vise grips. I the gripped the center pin and rotated it back and forth untill it was free from the rubber. Next I used a small screwdriver to pry the remaining rubber bushing out; it came out in one piece. It was that easy an that quick. On the smaller upper bushings. I just cut the inside rubber flange off and proceeded as before with "NO" drilling. The area between the center pin and the outer bushing housing is to small to drill. It worked awesome. I highly recomend this meathod to burnning or liquid nitrogen. Its cleaner, faster, and doesn't smell near as bad.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||10
